  "notes": {
    "arabic": "There is none to set. A language-detect pass over every 3s window of the source came back English throughout; the only Arabic is 'ibad Allah, after the out-point, opening his next section.",
    "marks": "The ochre bar goes under what each sentence turns on: Tawheed, more important, intention, people before, out the window, renew our intention, nobody, watching you.",
    "icons": "He gives the same two acts twice -- reading the Qur'an and praying -- first with people watching, then with nobody there. The drawn marks say it the same way: a rehal and a mihrab, each with the watchers beside it; then the watchers leave as he says 'nobody'; then the rehal and the mihrab again, alone. No mark stands for Allah's seeing -- the last line is words only, the largest on the reel.",
    "tally": "The number of prayers is a tally that draws on one stroke per word as he counts it up, and dims as he says it does not matter.",
    "window": "Everything else goes out the window: three ochre strokes leave through it as he says so.",
    "lineBreaks": "Every caption is split into explicit lines where the sense breaks, and judged against the real layout by check-wraps.mjs -- left to wrap on its own, four of them stranded a word ('something.', 'around,', 'us,', 'wrong,')."
  }
